{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"arterial-bilineate-vampirebat","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## The problem\n\nThe operator has adopted option (a) of bug `f850-674c-c89f-4b97` (`unsuited-locustal-incatern`):\n**Windows IS a declared support target for rebar.** That decision currently lives only in epic\n`55da-cee1-e556-4735` (`simple-brotherly-peacock`) and in the bug's comment trail. It creates\nstanding obligations on all future work under `src/rebar` — no unguarded POSIX-only syscall, no\nPOSIX mode bits as a security property, no locale-default text encoding at an I/O boundary — and\nthose obligations need a citable home in the tree, not only in a ticket.\n\nThe decomposition agent drafted `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md` (155 lines,\nstatus Proposed) plus its `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` marker and a regenerated `README.md`, but left\nthem UNCOMMITTED in a scratch worktree at `/Users/joeoakhart/adr-windows-support-target/`. A\ncleanup of that directory loses the draft. This task recovers and lands it.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Do change:**\n- add `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md` (status Proposed)\n- add the `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` reservation marker\n- regenerate `docs/adr/README.md` with `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` — never hand-edit it\n\n**Do NOT change:** `.github/workflows/test.yml` (that is S10,\n`arbitrary-nautical-spreadwing`), `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` (that is S1,\n`friendless-alabaster-cub`), or `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` (that is S11).\n\n## Second-pair-of-eyes obligation\n\nThe draft is a first draft and must be reviewed against the epic's measured evidence rather than\nadopted as written. Any assertion the evidence contradicts is corrected before landing, and the\ncorrection is recorded as a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Proving commands\n\n```\npython scripts/check_adr_numbers.py                       # bijection: markers <-> ADR files\npython scripts/gen_adr_index.py && git diff --exit-code docs/adr/README.md   # index is generated, not hand-edited\nuv run --no-sync pytest -k \"adr\" -m \"not integration and not external\" -q -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md` exists on `main` with status `Proposed`, and\n   states that Windows is a declared support target.\n2. `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` exists and `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0 — markers and ADR\n   files remain in bijection.\n3. `docs/adr/README.md` lists 0117 and is byte-identical to a fresh `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` run\n   (i.e. it was generated, not hand-edited).\n4. Every factual assertion in the ADR that cites a line number, a file, a commit, a job duration or\n   a failure count has been re-verified against the tree or the cited CI run at landing time, and\n   any that did not hold is corrected. Corrections are recorded as a comment on this ticket.\n5. No file outside `docs/adr/` is touched by this change.\n","id":"a01e-01e7-6e6e-4809","parent_id":"55da-cee1-e556-4735","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","adr","docs"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"S0: land ADR 0117 recording Windows as a declared support target"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788573351012167245,"uuid":"c1cf8e93-9035-4f2b-9ff0-c19d09a18e86"}